    "Notes!about": {
      "text": "# Boreas urban drive\n\n20 seconds near a busy Toronto intersection.\nCamera · LiDAR · radar · GPS · IMU\nPlay, seek, or explore the sensor tabs.\n\nCC BY 4.0 — Keenan Burnett et al.\nUniversity of Toronto\nhttps://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\nhttps://www.boreas.utias.utoronto.ca/\n\nBoreas: A Multi-Season Autonomous Driving Dataset\nKeenan Burnett, David J. Yoon, Yuchen Wu, Andrew Z. Li, Haowei\nZhang, Shichen Lu, Jingxing Qian, Wei-Kang Tseng, Andrew\nLambert, Keith Y. K. Leung, Angela P. Schoellig, and Timothy D.\nBarfoot\n\nAdapted for Lichtblick:\n20 seconds starting 170 seconds into `boreas-2021-09-02-11-42`;\ncamera sampled at 10 Hz, resized to 1280 × 1070 and H.265\nencoded (no B-frames, one-second GOPs, repeated VPS/SPS/PPS);\nLiDAR sampled at 5 Hz with every fourth point retained,\ncoordinates rounded to under 3 cm and 8-bit intensity. Radar at\n4 Hz is shown as a JPEG polar intensity image: horizontal axis\nis range (0.1192 m per bin, original bins averaged in pairs),\nvertical axis is azimuth sample index. Recorded 200 Hz IMU and 10 Hz postprocessed GPS\nare included. GPS latitude/longitude are converted from radians\nto degrees; altitude retains the dataset’s relative datum, not\nheight above sea level. Recorded poses and velocities are\nincluded, with a shifted local origin. Original sensor\ntimestamps are retained. No additional LiDAR motion compensation\nis applied. Camera and LiDAR are independent views; no projected\noverlays are included. Original sensor extrinsics are included\nas static transforms. IMU axes follow the Applanix source\nconvention; acceleration is the supplied processed acceleration,\nnot raw accelerometer output.\n\nPaper: https://doi.org/10.1177/02783649231160195\nAttribution is also embedded in the MCAP metadata.\nNo endorsement by the dataset authors is implied.\n"
    },
